    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d343">

                <pb facs="0549" n="263" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg263"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2661</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-07T16:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 7, 1916, 4 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 8, 6.30 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3857. Your 2976.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d343-f1"/> The circular in question came to
                    me at Headquarters <hi rendition="#italic">en clair</hi> on Saturday, April 29.
                    I sent telegram which came through the Foreign Office to the Chancellor in order
                    that he might take a copy. Later the Chancellor asked Grew to try to punctuate
                    and correct both the original telegram and his copy. The Chancellor <pb
                        facs="0550" n="264" xml:id="pg264"/> asked if Foreign Office had a copy. His
                    adjutant and son-in-law, Count Zech, went out of room to telephone and returned
                    saying Foreign Office had a copy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
